# Markets UI

Read `AGENTS.md` for full context. Critical layout rules:

## Ticket widget

- Ticket `<aside id="ticket">` lives **inside** `.page-shell` as grid column 2 (sibling of `.layout`).
- Desktop (`min-width: 1101px`): `.page-shell` is a 2-col CSS grid; ticket is `position: sticky` in column 2. No JS positioning.
- `body { overflow-x: clip }` (NOT `hidden`) — `hidden` creates a scroll container that breaks sticky.
- Mobile (`max-width: 1100px`): grid collapses to 1 col; ticket becomes fixed bottom sheet + FAB; `setTicketOpen()` mobile-only.
- Layout presets: `wide` widens ticket column; `feed`/`hide-ticket` collapse to single column.

## Theme engine

- Themes are **complete design systems**, defined as recipes in `lib/theme-engine.js` (`THEME_RECIPES`).
- `renderThemeCss(preset, config)` expands a recipe into scoped `body.theme-<id>` CSS covering material, geometry, depth, motion, and per-component states (nav, cards, market buttons, chips, inputs, primary/fab, modal, skeletons, scrollbar, focus).
- `themeCss()` in `lib/config.js` emits base `:root` + structural layout, then the engine layer.
- `THEME_PRESETS` in `lib/themes.js` stays the admin/server preset registry (label/concept/desc/config).
- Never reduce a theme to color + font + radius. A theme must be distinguishable in grayscale (geometry, shadow model, motion, component construction).

## CSS cascade

`styles.css` then `/api/theme.css`. Theme layer is scoped by `body.theme-<id>` (wins base specificity); desktop/mobile breakpoints must be explicit.

## Live data (`markets.js`)

- Today: WebSocket overview (`join-liveSportOverview`), not REST daterange for card odds.
- Use per-sport market slugs (`totals`, `handicap`, `totals_new`, etc.), not soccer-only defaults.

## Responsive checks

Verify ~1400px desktop and ~390px mobile after layout changes; test with a heavy-shadow theme.
